Venetium 0067 - every Lumia GPU (Qualcomm Adreno): no GPU timer queries, ANGLE's D3D11 backend keeps to feature level 9_x, GPU raster on all Lumia ids.
1. The Lumia 735's GPU process crashed 1-2 s after start in qcdx9um8974.dll (9.14.1140): 3 dumps out of 3 at the same
   address, writing past the end of a buffer. The crashing thread's stack memory gives the caller: viz
   SkiaOutputDeviceGL::Present -> GLSurfacePresentationHelper::PreSwapBuffers -> GPUTimer::QueryTimeStamp ->
   glBeginQueryEXT(GL_TIME_ELAPSED_EXT) -> ANGLE Query11::resume -> ID3D11DeviceContext::Begin(D3D11_QUERY_
   TIMESTAMP_DISJOINT) -> D3D10Level9 -> qcdx9um8974 (D3D11 at 9_x runs through the D3D9 user-mode driver), so the
   first presented frame; after 3 crashes Chromium turns the GPU off. A new gpu_driver_bug_list entry (487) drops
   GL_EXT_disjoint_timer_query for these GPUs, like upstream entry 112 for Android Adreno 3xx: the presentation helper
   then uses a fence (a D3D11 event query) and WebGL stops offering the timer extensions.
2. The 735's chrome://gpu also shows "Error allocating BlendState" (HRESULT 0x80070057) before every crash. ANGLE's
   D3D11 backend offers EXT_blend_func_extended at every feature level and Skia blends LCD text and coverage with
   dual-source factors whenever it is there, but 9_x has no dual-source blending. Checked against the D3D11 runtime
   (WARP at 9_3 and 9_1): a 9_x device rejects blend states with D3D11_BLEND_SRC1_*, IndependentBlendEnable or
   AlphaToCoverageEnable, and rasterizer states with DepthClipEnable FALSE. At 9_x ANGLE now offers neither
   EXT_blend_func_extended nor EXT_depth_clamp, drops alpha-to-coverage, and leaves IndependentBlendEnable off when
   the bound render targets share one blend description (per-buffer blend state needs 10_1 and is not offered
   there). _M_ARM only, like 0065: only ARM32 builds change, and only a device at 9_x takes the new paths.
3. The device ids come from the Lumia GPU drivers' INFs in github.com/WOA-Project/Lumia-Drivers: an ACPI display
   adapter's DXGI ids are its ACPI hardware id read as little-endian fourccs, so ACPI\QCOM246F = vendor 0x4d4f4351 +
   device 0x46363432, the id d3dprobe measured on the Adreno 330 and the 735's chrome://gpu shows for its Adreno
   305. 246F is the GPU of every Lumia from Windows Phone 8.1 on (8974, 8x26, 8x12, 8909, 8992, 8994: the 2520,
   1520, 930, 735, 830, 550, 650, 950, 950 XL ...), which 0051's GPU-raster exception already covered; the two
   Windows Phone 8.0 chips are added to it: 8960 (QCOM2002 -> 0x32303032: 920, 1020) and 8930 / 8x27 (QCOM0300 ->
   0x30303330: 520, 620, 720).

